00:45:57.040 --> 00:45:57.480
About Herman?

00:45:57.680 --> 00:45:59.980
Yes. He fell into the devil's...

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:08.640
well in the cave. He's dead? Dead as a doornail. This ends our troubles Carl. The vampire's dead.

00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:17.060
I can feel it in my bones. Well your bones may be wrong. What time did this happen? Quite early

00:46:17.060 --> 00:46:21.870
about nine o'clock. The cave is nearly two hours from here. That's why we didn't hear it sooner.

00:46:23.380 --> 00:46:27.840
Well it may interest you to know that there's been another death after your vampire died.

00:46:30.190 --> 00:46:31.470
Dr. von Neumann's housekeeper.

00:46:32.020 --> 00:46:33.580
Right here in her own room.

00:46:33.720 --> 00:46:35.020
Mother of mercy.

00:46:35.620 --> 00:46:36.600
What are we going to do?

00:46:36.860 --> 00:46:38.960
Well, a natural death wouldn't kill a vampire, Carl.

00:46:39.710 --> 00:46:40.870
You know the accepted theory?

00:46:41.390 --> 00:46:42.770
A stake driven through the heart?

00:46:43.400 --> 00:46:43.900
Oh, yes.

00:46:43.920 --> 00:46:45.100
That's the theory, all right.

00:46:45.220 --> 00:46:46.060
But, but, but.

00:46:46.540 --> 00:46:46.920
But what?

00:46:47.200 --> 00:46:47.960
But they did.

00:46:48.900 --> 00:46:50.780
They drove a stake through his heart.

00:46:51.340 --> 00:46:51.960
Good God.

00:46:52.100 --> 00:46:53.160
Are we living in the Middle Ages?

00:46:53.280 --> 00:46:55.120
It wasn't through my sanction, Carl.

00:46:55.880 --> 00:46:56.740
Basawa did it.

00:46:57.260 --> 00:46:58.360
He told me so himself.

00:47:00.990 --> 00:47:03.770
Well, that ends the vampire theory as far as I'm concerned.

00:47:04.500 --> 00:47:07.920
Herman Gleib died in the accepted fashion for killing a vampire.

00:47:08.860 --> 00:47:11.160
Oh, no, there's some human agency at work here, Doctor.

00:47:11.620 --> 00:47:15.940
A madman who kills to satisfy some violent, sadistic urge.

00:47:16.120 --> 00:47:17.380
Yes, you're right, Carl.

00:47:18.030 --> 00:47:20.290
I've been a fool, a superstitious fool.

00:47:22.620 --> 00:47:23.760
Did they leave his body in the cave?

00:47:24.240 --> 00:47:26.140
Yes. Yes, they did.

00:47:27.490 --> 00:47:29.970
Well, in view of what's happened, don't you think you owe him a decent burial?

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:35.430
You're right. In view of what has happened, we do owe him that, Carl.

00:47:35.900 --> 00:47:37.840
I'll see to it at once this very instant,

00:47:38.060 --> 00:47:41.610
and I'll make arrangements for Georgiana's removal to the morgue.

00:47:41.970 --> 00:47:44.550
Good night, Doctor. Pardon the intrusion.

00:47:44.650 --> 00:47:45.310
Good night, Gustav.

00:47:45.350 --> 00:47:46.250
Pardon the intrusion.

00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:54.250
Here I am, just where I started weeks ago.

00:47:55.440 --> 00:47:58.860
There isn't a single theory that doesn't lead straight into a stone wall.

00:48:00.640 --> 00:48:04.760
I've jested about this vampire business because my better judgment told me it was a lot of nonsense.

00:48:05.800 --> 00:48:08.320
Then I reached the point where I was willing to accept even that.

00:48:09.520 --> 00:48:11.320
Because it seemed to satisfy the equation.

00:48:12.160 --> 00:48:13.400
All of it would be superstitious.

00:48:15.420 --> 00:48:16.540
I don't know which way to turn.

00:48:17.380 --> 00:48:17.960
Where to look?

00:48:18.020 --> 00:48:18.760
What to look for?

00:48:20.540 --> 00:48:22.640
Why should anyone want human blood?

00:48:23.420 --> 00:48:23.760
Why?

00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:24.300
Why?

00:48:24.640 --> 00:48:25.740
Calm yourself, Carl.

00:48:26.490 --> 00:48:27.170
Calm myself.

00:48:27.980 --> 00:48:29.970
Calm myself with all these dumb sol...

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:39.710
murder staring me in the face and no solution in sight how much blood is there in the human body

00:48:39.710 --> 00:48:46.710
doctor about six liters approximately can you think of any purpose for which that amount of

00:48:46.710 --> 00:48:56.190
blood might be used no not even in transfusions the point which stops me there isn't any other

00:48:56.190 --> 00:48:57.290
use for human blood.

00:49:00.190 --> 00:49:06.120
murderers leave clues and these atrocities are murders doctor those simple fools in the village

00:49:06.120 --> 00:49:10.200
can believe what they like but you and i are same thinking people and you know and i know doctor

00:49:10.200 --> 00:49:17.920
that these are murders the last one was done here in this very house right under this roof

00:49:17.920 --> 00:49:26.110
all right i'll start here i'm going over every foot of this place both inside and out nobody

00:49:26.110 --> 00:49:29.650
Sane or insane is clever enough to get away with murder without leaving a clue of some sort.

00:49:30.120 --> 00:49:31.760
And I'm going to find that clue, Cump.

00:49:32.290 --> 00:49:33.610
You mustn't let your nerves run away with you.

00:49:34.320 --> 00:49:34.640
Here.

00:49:36.100 --> 00:49:41.840
These, these will help to give you a good night's sleep.

00:49:45.280 --> 00:49:48.230
If there are any clues, they'll be here in the morning

00:49:48.230 --> 00:49:52.500
when your nerves are calm and your mind is clear.

00:49:53.130 --> 00:49:55.620
Take my advice and go home to rest.

00:49:55.800 --> 00:49:57.560
I imagine the thousand demons were after me

00:49:57.560 --> 00:49:58.680
as I came down those stairs.

00:49:59.200 --> 00:49:59.980
Oh, didn't I tell you?

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:04.610
to stay in your room yes but i wanted the doctor to come up and quiet auntie you know it isn't her

00:50:04.610 --> 00:50:10.140
imagination this time of course i'll come right away take my advice young man go home and go to

00:50:10.140 --> 00:50:25.220
bed good night carl good night rose good night god good night doctor

00:51:41.000 --> 00:51:49.270
If his lights are on, you must wait, Emil, wait until he has gone to bed.

00:53:34.480 --> 00:53:36.380
Handle him as you did the others, Emil.

00:53:36.640 --> 00:53:43.280
Strong, very strong.

00:53:48.070 --> 00:53:53.380
I am waiting for you, waiting for you to bring him to the laboratory.

00:54:34.188 --> 00:54:34.688
You!

00:54:35.532 --> 00:54:36.532
You're the one!

00:54:37.132 --> 00:54:38.332
What mad thing are you doing?

00:54:38.432 --> 00:54:38.732
Mad.

00:54:39.660 --> 00:54:42.060
Is one who has solved the secret of life to be considered mad?

00:54:42.700 --> 00:54:43.100
Life.

00:54:43.916 --> 00:54:44.816
Created in the laboratory.

00:54:45.836 --> 00:54:47.316
No mere christening growth.

00:54:47.532 --> 00:54:48.032
a tissue.

00:54:48.620 --> 00:54:50.620
living, growing tissue.

00:54:50.668 --> 00:54:51.068
Like.

00:54:51.500 --> 00:54:52.840
that moves, pulsates.

00:54:53.196 --> 00:54:55.276
and demands food for its continued growth.

00:54:56.204 --> 00:54:56.404
Yeah.

00:54:57.420 --> 00:54:58.400
You shuddering horror.

00:54:59.500 --> 00:54:59.980
So did I.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:01.000
the first time.

00:55:01.532 --> 00:55:05.372
But what will a few lies be weighed in the balance against the achievement of biological science?

00:55:05.916 --> 00:55:06.176
Thank you.

00:55:08.028 --> 00:55:08.868
I've lifted the bane.

00:55:09.884 --> 00:55:10.964
I have created life.

00:55:12.028 --> 00:55:13.348
Arrested the secret of life.

00:55:13.532 --> 00:55:14.092
from life.

00:55:14.240 --> 00:55:15.120
Now do you understand?

00:55:15.580 --> 00:55:19.440
For the lives of those who have gone before, I have created life!

00:55:20.604 --> 00:55:21.404
Hotel Kong!

00:55:23.292 --> 00:55:23.792
You may.

00:55:25.564 --> 00:55:28.164
For tonight, Carl's name will be added to yours.

00:55:29.404 --> 00:55:29.964
I'm old.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:32.880
All of those who miss achievement will immortalize.

00:57:06.170 --> 00:57:08.110
I didn't take your sleeping tablets, doctor.

00:57:46.730 --> 00:57:52.550
here. He's the one who murdered them. Stay where you are. You'll have a chance to tell everything, doctor.

00:58:05.120 --> 00:58:07.590
Take care of our demon. Get her out of here.

00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:52.650
You stay here, Neiman and Damian.

00:58:58.200 --> 00:58:59.080
She mustn't see them.

00:59:02.810 --> 00:59:04.570
Where is Dr. Veneon? I must see him immediately.

00:59:05.110 --> 00:59:08.080
I'm guessing you can't. He can't be disturbed.

00:59:08.450 --> 00:59:09.890
Oh, but I must see him. I simply must.

00:59:10.500 --> 00:59:14.600
That hydrous magnesium sulfate he gave me is affecting me most peculiarly.

00:59:16.120 --> 00:59:17.020
You'll pardon me?

00:59:21.310 --> 00:59:22.970
Hydrous magnesium sulfate?

00:59:25.300 --> 00:59:26.400
Well, that's Epsom salts.

00:59:31.210 --> 00:59:31.450
Thank you.
